{
  "rationale": "The plant separates sensing (obstacle events) and motion (controllable actions). The specification encodes a conservative, coverage-oriented exploration policy: random_walk is used in clear states for coverage, move_forward is used only in a short commit state, and recovery from obstacles is handled by short directed turns or, as a last resort, a full_rotate. All obstacle events force immediate recovery, and only one controllable is enabled per state to avoid oscillations.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion; all events are atomic.",
    "Specification encodes: (1) random_walk in clear/search, (2) move_forward only in a commit state, (3) rotate_clockwise for obs_front/obs_left, rotate_counterclockwise for obs_right, (4) full_rotate only after repeated obstacles, (5) rapid return to exploration after path_clear."
  ],
